earth: you are one of the rescue station's best-known people: the town wants to close its night post and the station asks you to speak for it
gap: 3-8
scene: The town wants to close the rescue station's night post to save money, and there is a public meeting on Thursday. {boss}, who runs the station, asks {N} to speak for {place}: people trust {N}, and {N} has been out on enough nights to say what the post is for. The council will be on the stage, and the papers in the front row.
scene W: The post exists for everyone in the town, including the ones who will never know they needed it; someone should say so.
scene U: {N} knows the call-out times, and the times show what the post is worth better than any speech.
scene B: A full hall and the papers in the front row: whoever saves the night post will be remembered for it.
scene R: {N} remembers the night on the ice, and the faces in the hall should feel what that night was like.
scene G: The families the post has helped over the years are the ones whose word should count most.
- W | speak, and set out plainly what the post has done, call by call | lever: loyalty | v: universalism, security | foot: place prot.rescue | chance: 75
- U | agree, and bring the response times for every night of the last five years | lever: loyalty | v: achievement | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- B | speak, and ask for a seat on whatever review comes after | lever: office | v: power, achievement | foot: person patron | chance: 60
- R | speak from the heart about the night on the ice, and let the hall feel it | lever: lead | v: stimulation, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 65
- G | decline the stage, and ask the families the post has helped to speak instead | lever: exit | v: benevolence, tradition | foot: person neighbour | chance: 80
- W>B | speak for the post, and propose a smaller night crew that still covers the town | lever: voice | v: security, power | foot: door kept your word | chance: 65
- U>R | write it all down for the station's head to read out, and stay off the stage | lever: loyalty | v: self-direction, security | foot: person boss | chance: 80
- B>G | speak, and see that the old families in the front rows are thanked by name | lever: lead | v: power, tradition | foot: person elder | chance: 70
- R>W | turn the meeting into a rally, and call on everyone to sign the petition | lever: lead | v: stimulation, universalism | foot: place rule.voice | chance: 60
- G>U | say no: the station's head knows the work better and should speak | lever: exit | v: tradition, security | foot: means time+.04 | chance: 90
works: The council puts the closure off for a year, and the post's lights stay on through the winter.
works: For weeks afterwards strangers at the shops tell {N} they were in the hall that night.
fails: The council closes the night post anyway, by two votes, and the hall empties in silence.
fails: The paper prints one clumsy sentence of {Ns} and nothing else, and it follows {N} around for a while.

