== the Saturday food drive
tier: everyday
stages: young_adult adult mature elder
age: 18-90
calls: WG
rate: 1
tone: mixed
life: community
horizon: months
roles: colleague, neighbour, boss
cast_want: asked_help
sphere: care
earth: you help out at the charity: they ask you to give your Saturdays to the winter food drive
gap: 3-8
scene: The charity at {place} runs a food drive every Saturday through the winter, and since two of the regulars moved away there is a gap on the rota. {colleague} asks {N}, a little shyly, over the tea urn: could {N} give Saturdays until spring, sorting the tins, packing the boxes, driving them round?
scene W: Somebody has to fill the gap, and the families waiting on the boxes do not care whose turn it was.
scene U: The stockroom is a muddle of tins and dates, and {N} can see how much better it could run.
scene B: Saturdays are worth something to {N}, and it is fair to ask what giving them would bring.
scene R: A whole winter of Saturdays in a cold hall sounds like a long time, unless it can be fun.
scene G: The drive has always run on neighbours helping neighbours, and {N} is one of them now.
- W | give every Saturday until spring, and turn up on time | lever: loyalty | v: benevolence, conformity | foot: place gather.hall | chance: 85
- U | say yes, and sort out the stock list so nothing goes past its date | lever: loyalty | v: achievement, security | foot: mark learned a skill | chance: 80
- B | give two Saturdays a month, and ask for a say in how the boxes are shared | lever: voice | v: power, self-direction | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- R | skip the rota, and drop in on the mornings that feel right | lever: neglect | v: hedonism, self-direction | foot: means freedom+.04 | chance: 90
- G | say yes, and bring the household along to pack the boxes | lever: loyalty | v: benevolence, tradition | foot: means ties+.05 | chance: 80
- W>R | sign up, and start a Saturday breakfast for the volunteers too | lever: loyalty | v: benevolence, hedonism | foot: person friend | chance: 75
- U>G | take the van round the outlying farms, where nobody knows the drive exists | lever: loyalty | v: universalism, benevolence | foot: door helped someone in need | chance: 70
- B>W | decline the Saturdays, and get the workplace to give a month of stock | lever: voice | v: benevolence, power | foot: person boss | chance: 60
- R>U | put out a lively appeal on the local radio, and count what comes in | lever: voice | v: stimulation, achievement | foot: person go-between | chance: 65
- G>B | say no: Saturdays belong to home, and home needs them | lever: exit | v: tradition, security | foot: means time+.05 | chance: 95
works: By spring the drive has never missed a Saturday, and the boxes go out fuller than last year.
works: {colleague} saves {N} a seat by the tea urn every week, and the two of them become a fixture of the place.
fails: The cold hall and the early starts wear thin, and by February the gap on the rota is back.
fails: A van breaks down on the busiest Saturday, and twenty households wait for boxes that come a day late.

