- U | take it on, and bring in a nurse each month to answer the hard questions | lever: lead | lead: knowing | v: achievement, benevolence | foot: person colleague | chance: 70
- B | agree, if the clinic pays for the room and puts the group in its leaflet | lever: voice | v: power, security | foot: person patron | chance: 60
- R | say no: holding everyone else's worries every week is too much just now | lever: exit | v: self-direction | foot: means health+.04 | chance: 90
- G | carry it on as she ran it, the same chairs and the same biscuits | lever: loyalty | v: tradition, benevolence | foot: person friend | chance: 85
- W>G | take it on, and ring every member who has stopped coming | lever: lead | lead: rules | v: benevolence, conformity | foot: door helped someone in need | chance: 75
- U>W | run it for a year while writing down how it works, for whoever comes next | lever: loyalty | v: security, achievement | foot: lesson write it down for later | chance: 75
- B>U | decline the running of it, but find a grant for a paid organiser | lever: voice | v: achievement, power | foot: means time+.03 | chance: 55
- R>B | take it on, and grow it into the biggest carers' group in town | lever: lead | lead: inspiring | v: stimulation, achievement | foot: place care.houses | chance: 60
- G>R | share it with two of the others, taking turns, as friends do | lever: loyalty | v: benevolence, hedonism | foot: person regular | chance: 80
works: The Tuesdays go on, a little different and just as full, and the founder writes from her new town to say she heard.
works: A newcomer who sat silent for weeks finally speaks one evening, and {N} knows why the group matters.
fails: Attendance drops by half in the first season, and {N} spends Tuesdays wondering what changed.
