== how the watch walks the town at night
tier: decision
cast_want: decide
sphere: prot
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
tone: mixed
life: community, work
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague, rival
earth: the watch must settle how it covers the town after dark, and {N} has the say
scene: After a winter of break-ins on the east side, the watch at {place} is rethinking how it covers the town at night. There are only so many officers and so many hours. {boss} has asked {N} to decide the new plan, and whatever {N} chooses will be how the town is walked for years.
- W | fixed patrols on every street, the same for every ward | v: universalism, security | scope: town_sphere | chance: 70
- U | send the patrols where the figures show the trouble is | v: achievement, security | scope: town_sphere | chance: 70
- B | let traders who pay towards it have extra patrols on their streets | v: power, security | scope: town_sphere | chance: 65
- G | bring back officers who walk the same streets for years and know the families | v: tradition, benevolence | scope: town_sphere | chance: 65
works: The break-ins fall off by spring, and people on the east side start leaving their lights off again.
works: {colleague} says the night shifts have never run so smoothly.
fails: The trouble simply moves to the streets the patrols do not cover, and the letters follow it.
fails: {rival} calls the plan a waste of good officers, and the council starts asking the same.

== who goes out with the rescue team
tier: decision
cast_want: decide
sphere: prot
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
tone: mixed
life: community, health
horizon: years
roles: colleague, boss, rival
earth: the rescue team has more volunteers than it can safely send, and {N} must set how it takes people on
scene: The rescue team at {place} has twice as many willing volunteers as it can safely send out, and two near misses this year. The old hands want stricter rules, the new ones want to be useful now, and the treasurer says the team cannot go on unpaid much longer. {N} has been asked to set how the team takes people on.
- W | every volunteer passes the full course before going out on a call | v: conformity, security | scope: place | chance: 75
- R | take anyone willing, and train them on the calls themselves | v: stimulation, benevolence | scope: place | chance: 55
- B | keep a small paid crew, funded by fees on rescues from closed paths | v: achievement, power | scope: place | chance: 60
works: A year on, the team goes out with more confidence than it ever has, and there have been no more near misses.
works: {colleague} tells the newcomers that the way they are taken on now is the best thing that happened to the team.
fails: Half the volunteers drift away in the first season, unhappy with the change.
fails: {rival} says the team has lost what made it special, and a few of the old hands agree.

== the watch at the march
tier: decision
cast_want: decide
sphere: prot
stages: adult mature elder
age: 25-90
tone: mixed
life: community, work
horizon: months
roles: boss, colleague, rival
earth: a large march is coming through town, and {N} must plan how the watch will handle it
scene: A large march is coming through the town centre next month, over the closing of the works, and feelings are high on both sides. The watch has to decide how to handle it, and {boss} has handed the plan to {N}. The way it goes will be remembered, by the marchers and by the shopkeepers, long after the day.
- W | police the march by the book, with the same rules as every march | v: conformity, universalism | scope: town_sphere | chance: 70
- U | meet the organisers beforehand, and plan the route from what is known | v: security, achievement | scope: town_sphere | chance: 70
- R | let the march go where it will, with officers walking alongside | v: self-direction, stimulation | scope: town_sphere | chance: 55
- G>W | ask the march's own stewards to keep order, with the watch at a distance | v: benevolence, conformity | scope: town_sphere | chance: 60
works: The march passes through loud and peaceful, and both sides say afterwards that the watch got it right.
works: The marchers' organiser sends {N} a short note of thanks, which {boss} pins on the board.
fails: A scuffle by the square makes the evening news, and everyone has an opinion on whose fault it was.
fails: The shopkeepers say they were left exposed, and {rival} takes up their complaint.

== who oversees the watch
tier: decision
cast_want: decide
sphere: prot
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-90
tone: mixed
life: community, work
horizon: years
roles: boss, colleague, rival
earth: the government is drawing up new rules on who checks the watch's work, and asks for {N}'s view
scene: A row over a mishandled complaint in another town has reached the national papers, and the government is drawing up new rules on who checks the watch's work. {N} is known well beyond the town now, and the review has asked for {Ns} view. Whatever {N} says will be quoted in the assembly.
- U>W | back a national review board that publishes every complaint and its outcome | v: universalism, achievement | scope: nation | chance: 45
- B | keep oversight inside the force, where the chiefs answer for it | v: power, security | scope: town_sphere | chance: 65
- G | let each town's own council oversee its own watch | v: tradition, security | scope: town_sphere | chance: 65
works: The review's report quotes {N} on its first page, and the town's watch adopts the same way ahead of the law.
works: {colleague} says the officers trust the new arrangement more than anyone expected.
fails: The review goes another way entirely, and {Ns} evidence is a footnote.
fails: {rival} says {N} has turned on the watch, and some of the officers believe it.

