horizon: years
roles: colleague, boss, rival
earth: the clinic's waiting list is eleven weeks long, and the board gives {N} the say on who is seen first
scene: The waiting list at {place} has grown to eleven weeks, and everyone has an idea of what to do about it. The staff are tired, the patients are angry, and the board has given {N} the say on how the clinic decides who is seen first. Whatever {N} chooses, the other clinics across town will be watching to see if it works.
- W | see patients strictly by need, as the clinic's written rules define it | v: universalism, conformity | scope: place | chance: 70
- U | sort every patient by a scored assessment, and publish how it works | v: achievement, universalism | scope: place | chance: 65
- B | open a paid evening list, and let its fees shorten the day list | v: achievement, power | scope: place | chance: 60
- R | open two walk-in afternoons a week, first come, first seen | v: self-direction, benevolence | scope: place | chance: 60
works: By the end of the year the list is down to five weeks, and the other clinics ask how it was done.
works: {colleague} says the waiting room feels calmer than it has in years.
fails: The list shrinks for a season and then grows back, and the board asks {N} what went wrong.
fails: {rival} tells the local paper the change has made things worse, and the phones ring all week.

