earth: the care home's board asks {N} to decide how the residents' days will run
scene: The care home at {place} is being asked to change: the families want more freedom for their parents, the staff want the routines that keep everyone safe, and the budget will not stretch to both. The board has asked {N} to decide how the home's days will run.
- G | keep the old routines: meals at set hours, the same faces on every shift | v: tradition, security | scope: place | chance: 75
- R | let residents set their own hours, outings and visits | v: self-direction, hedonism | scope: place | chance: 55
- B>G | take paying residents to fund more staff in the shared rooms | v: power, benevolence | scope: place | chance: 60
works: The residents settle into the new days, and one of the families sends the staff flowers.
works: {colleague} says the home has not felt so much like a home in years.
fails: The staff struggle with the change, and two of the best leave before the year is out.
